{"results":[{"url":"https://politifact.com/personalities/bernie-sanders/","final_url":"https://politifact.com/personalities/bernie-sanders/","title":"Bernie Sanders – PolitiFact","description":null,"language":"en","text":"# Bernie Sanders\n\nBernie Sanders is a senator from Vermont. Sanders was first elected to the Senate in 2007 and was re-elected in 2012 and 2018. The senator also ran an unsuccessful presidential campaign in 2016, losing the Democratic primary to Hillary Clinton. From 1991 until 2007, he was the representative of Vermont’s At-Large District of the House of Representatives. Sanders was the mayor of Burlington from 1981 to 1989. He received a bachelor’s degree in political science from the University of Chicago. In 2019, he announced he was running for the Democratic nomination for president and dropped out in April 2020.\n\nBernie Sanders Website\n\n## Scorecard\n\n##### true\n\n0%\n21 Checks\n\n##### mostly true\n\n0%\n64 Checks\n\n##### half true\n\n0%\n49 Checks\n\n##### mostly false\n\n0%\n28 Checks\n\n##### false\n\n0%\n19 Checks\n\n##### Pants on Fire\n\n0%\n0 Checks\n\nFor more details, see the \nPrinciples of PolitiFact\n\n## Latest Fact-Checks By Bernie Sanders\n\nBernie Sanders   \n\nstated on June 12, 2026 in an X post:\n\nBy\nCaleb McCullough\n•\n\nJune 17, 2026\n\n---\n\nBernie Sanders   \n\nstated on April 22, 2026 in a Senate committee hearing:\n\nBy\nAmy Sherman\n•\n\nApril 30, 2026\n\n---\n\nBernie Sanders   \n\nstated on May 12, 2025 in a post on X:\n\n---\n\nBernie Sanders   \n\nstated on January 2, 2025 in a statement to the media:\n\nBy\nAmy Sherman\n•\n\nJanuary 9, 2025\n\n---\n\nBernie Sanders   \n\nstated on November 10, 2024 in an interview on CNN's \"State of the Union\":\n\nBy\nLouis Jacobson\n•\n\nNovember 11, 2024\n\n---\n\nBernie Sanders   \n\nstated on September 17, 2023 in an interview on CNN's \"State of the Union\":\n\nBy\nLouis Jacobson, \nMatthew Crowley\n•\n\nSeptember 21, 2023\n\n---\n\nBernie Sanders   \n\nsta